.TH GIT-GET 1 "2026-11-23" "git-get" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
git-get \- clone a git repository into a directory tree under GETPATH
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B git-get
.RI [ options ]
.I repository
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B git-get
clones a repository to
.IR $GETPATH/host/path ,
in the style of
.IR "go get" .
For example,
.I github.com/owner/repo
is cloned to
.IR ~/src/github.com/owner/repo .
The resulting path is printed to standard output, so it can be used with
.BR cd .
.PP
If the destination already contains a
.I .git
file or directory, nothing is cloned, fetched, or pulled, and the existing path is
printed. If the destination exists without one, it is an error. The remote is
checked with
.B git ls\-remote
before any directory is created, so a missing or private repository leaves
nothing behind.
.PP
Progress is shown on standard error only when it is a terminal.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Print the git commands and their output to standard error. A lone
.B \-v
with no repository prints the version instead.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit. Git intercepts
.B git get \-\-help
to show this page, so use
.B \-h
for the usage text.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
Treat every following argument as a repository, even if it begins with a dash.
.PP
Options may appear before or after the repository. Unknown or duplicate options
and extra arguments are errors.
.B \-h
and
.B \-\-version
take precedence over everything else before
.BR \-\- .
.SH ARGUMENTS
.TP
.I repository
The repository to clone, in one of these forms:
.RS
.IP \(bu 4
.I host/owner/repo
.IP \(bu 4
.I https://host/owner/repo.git
.IP \(bu 4
.I ssh://git@host/owner/repo.git
.IP \(bu 4
.I git@host:owner/repo.git
.RE
.IP
The host is required. A trailing
.I .git
is removed from the directory. A port and any credentials are not part of the
directory. A bare
.I host/owner/repo
is cloned over HTTPS.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Exits 0 on success, including
.B \-h
and
.BR \-\-version .
Any error exits 1 and prints a line beginning
.B error:
to standard error. Nothing is printed to standard output on failure.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B GETPATH
Root directory for cloned repositories. It must be an absolute path, or begin
with
.I ~/
or be
.IR ~ .
Takes precedence over
.BR get.path .
.SH CONFIGURATION
.TP
.B get.path
Root directory for cloned repositories, read from the global git config and
used when
.B GETPATH
is not set. The default is
.IR ~/src .
.PP
.RS
.EX
git config \-\-global get.path ~/dev
.EE
.RE
.PP
To clone over SSH instead, rewrite the URL with
.BR url.<base>.insteadOf :
.PP
.RS
.EX
git config \-\-global url.ssh://git@github.com/.insteadOf https://github.com/
.EE
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.EX
$ git get github.com/owner/repo
~/src/github.com/owner/repo
$ git get https://github.com/owner/repo.git
~/src/github.com/owner/repo
$ git get git@github.com:owner/repo.git
~/src/github.com/owner/repo
$ GETPATH=~/corp git get github.com/org/repo
~/corp/github.com/org/repo
$ cd "$(git get github.com/owner/repo)"
$ git get \-v github.com/owner/repo
$ git get \-\- \-odd\-name
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR git\-clone (1)
